# Open a real audio backend through the device manager and confirm it runs.
#
#   app/ardop-spine --audio-null-device --script test/app/devices.script
#
# miniaudio's synthetic device gives a *real* backend with a real device thread,
# so this exercises the whole path -- the manager's state machine, the open, the
# platform bind, the block size the backend asked for, the credit -- on a machine
# with no sound card. Which is every CI runner.
#
# It is the binary half of test_devices: that suite drives the manager as a
# library, this proves the program built around it actually starts.

@echo opening the device

@wait secs=2
@stats

MYCALL N0AAA
ARQBW 2000MAX
LISTEN TRUE

@wait secs=2
@stats

# Nothing was transmitted, nothing was received, and nothing was lost.
@expect no-loss
